t-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Generate 20 distinct synthetic MP4 test clips using varying resolutions (720p, 1080p, 4K), non-standard variable frame rates (24.1 fps, 29.9 fps, 30.2 fps), and varied audio sample rates (44.1 kHz, 48 kHz). 2. Normalize each clip using scale=1920:1080:force_original_aspect_ratio=decrease,pad=1920:1080:(ow-iw)/2:(oh-ih)/2,setsar=1,fps=30, encoding to libx264 with -video[span_196](start_span)[span_196](end_span)_track_timescale 30000 and audio resampled to 48 kHz stereo.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Concatenate the normalized segments using -f concat -safe 0 -c [span_177](start_span)[span_177](end_span)copy.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:60pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Perform packet-level inspection via PyAV to verify packet presentation timestamps (PTS) across edit seams, and measure total output duration against the sum of source audio durations.</span></li></ol><ul class="lst-kix_list_14-0" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Evidence Required</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Complete f[span_10](start_span)[span_10](end_span)fprobe packet log verifying strictly monotonically increasing PTS/DTS values across all seam transitions; absolute cumulative drift &lt;1.0\text{ ms} across a 30-minute test sequence.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Success Criteria</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Zero stream warnings, zero Non-monotonous DTS terminal alerts, and zero perceptible audio-video desynchronization.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Why Research Evidence is Insufficient</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Published documentation notes that the concat demuxer works with identical streams, but real-world AI-generated clips frequently carry subtle container-level metadata quirks that require empirical stress-testing.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Experiment 2: libass Karaoke Highlight Performance vs. Remotion Chromium Overhead</span></h3><ul class="lst-kix_list_16-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom